---
import Layout from '../layouts/SimplePage.astro';
import CertificationBadge from '../components/CertificationBadge.astro';
import { certifications } from '../data/certifications';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="About Vaishakh G K"
>
    <center>
        <h1>I'm Vaishakh G K</h1>
        <p>
            Cybersecurity enthusiast with a strong foundation in software
            engineering, interested in understanding how systems work.
        </p>
    </center>

    <p>
        I'm passionate about cybersecurity and software engineering, with
        a particular interest in understanding how applications, networks,
        and systems work beneath the surface. I have a solid foundation in
        software development, with experience building web applications,
        backend services, APIs, databases, and distributed systems. This
        background gives me a practical understanding of how software is
        designed, developed, and deployed.
    </p>

    <p>
        My cybersecurity interests include application security,
        penetration testing, vulnerability analysis, Linux security,
        network security, and wireless security. I have a good understanding
        of security concepts, common attack techniques, and security tools.
        I enjoy understanding how weaknesses arise, how they can be exploited,
        and how systems can be better secured.
    </p>

    <p>
        I primarily work with Go and C, while also having experience with
        JavaScript and other web technologies. Beyond application development,
        I spend time exploring Linux, system internals, networking,
        low-level programming, and open-source software. I enjoy combining
        my development knowledge with security concepts to better understand
        and analyze the systems I work with.
    </p>

    <h2>Beyond Programming</h2>

    <p>
        I'm naturally curious about technology and enjoy exploring things
        beyond conventional software development. I spend a lot of time
        working with Linux, configuring and customizing my environment,
        exploring open-source security tools, experimenting with networking
        and hardware, and understanding the lower layers of computer systems.
    </p>

    <p>
        I enjoy hands-on learning, solving technical challenges, experimenting
        with tools, and documenting what I discover. I also write about
        technical concepts and share knowledge through my blog.
    </p>


	<h2>Why I Have This Website</h2>

	<p>
		This website is more than a portfolio. It's my personal space on the
		internet — a place to keep track of what I'm building, what I'm
		learning, and the things I find interesting.
	</p>

	<p>
		I want to write about the things I learn in a way that is useful to
		other people. If I spend several hours figuring out something that
		seemed confusing at first, I'd rather document it so that someone
		else can understand it a little faster.
	</p>

	<p>
		You'll find my projects, technical notes, experiments, cybersecurity
		writing, and other things I'm interested in here. Some of them will
		be polished projects, while others will simply be a record of
		something I wanted to explore.
	</p>

	<p>
		This site will probably change as I do. The technologies I use,
		the things I work on, and even my interests will change over time.
		The idea is simply to keep building, keep learning, and share some
		of that journey along the way.
	</p>

    <center><h2>Certifications & Badges</h2></center>
	<div class="certification-badges">
		{certifications.map((cert) => (
			<CertificationBadge
				name={cert.name}
				issuer={cert.issuer}
				credlyUrl={cert.credlyUrl}
				dateIssued={cert.dateIssued}
				expirationDate={cert.expirationDate}
				inProgress={cert.inProgress}
				badgeImageUrl={cert.badgeImageUrl}
			/>
		))}
	</div>

	<style>
		.certification-badges {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: repeat(
				auto-fit,
				minmax(min(100%, 280px), 1fr)
			);
			max-width: 900px;
			width: 100%;
			margin: 2rem auto;
			gap: 1rem;
			align-items: stretch;
		}

		.certification-badges > * {
			width: 100%;
			min-width: 0;
			box-sizing: border-box;
		}

		@media (max-width: 767px) {
			.certification-badges {
				grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			}
		}
	</style>

</Layout>